# Word Pop — project-wide standards

Applies to every **`*.word-pop.tsx`** page and **`client/src/lib/wordPopSpeak.ts`**.

## Canonical library — `@/lib/wordPopSpeak`

Do **not** pass **`balloon.word`** / **`currentWord.word`** (grid tokens like **`HI`**, **`NO`**, **`HOWAREYOU`**) directly to **`SpeechSynthesisUtterance`**. Raw grid keys garble phrases or trigger unwanted letter-by-letter reading for common words — route audio through **`speakWordPopAnswer`** so speak text is derived from the vocab **`file`** basename via **`getCrosswordSpeakText`** (typically lowercase for single-token files).

### Words vs spelled acronyms (**HI** vs **USA**)

There is a real conflict:

- **Greetings / short lexical words** (**HI**, **NO**, etc.) should sound like whole words. Using basename-derived lowercase (**`hi.png`** → “hi”) matches that goal.
- **Real acronyms** (**USA**, **UK**, **NASA** if spelled letter-by-letter in class) should **not** automatically become lowercase — the engine would say “usa” as a word instead of **U‑S‑A**.

**Agent / contributor workflow**

1. When adding or changing vocabulary where the grid token is **short**, **all caps**, or **could be either a word or an acronym**, **stop and ask the curriculum owner** which TTS behavior they want (spoken word vs spelled letters), unless the project has already adopted an explicit per-entry flag or naming convention for that item.
2. Do **not** assume one global rule covers every future item; treating **USA** like **HI** without confirmation is wrong for typical classroom acronym pronunciation.

Until a coded convention exists (e.g. optional **`ttsSpellLetters`** / **`speakAs`** on vocab rows implemented in **`wordPopSpeak`**), acronym pronunciation is **product/editorial**, not something to infer from token shape alone.

| Helper | Use |
|--------|-----|
| **`getWordPopDisplayWord(gridWord, imageFile, turkish?)`** | Banner labels, balloons, any learner-visible English derived from the vocab row. Uses **`getSpellQuestDisplayWord`** (basename → spaced uppercase) plus optional closing punctuation (below). |
| **`getWordPopSpeakText(gridWord, imageFile, turkish?)`** | Same phrase logic as speech, lowercase for TTS (via **`getCrosswordSpeakText`**). Underscores in basenames are turned into spaces for reading. |
| **`speakWordPopAnswer(gridWord, imageFile, turkish?, options?)`** | Default pronunciation path after correct pops / hint speaker. Prefer **`entry.file`** + **`entry.turkish`** from the **`vocabulary`** row matching **`gridWord`**. |

### Speech rate

**`speakWordPopAnswer`** defaults to **`rate: 0.8`** (primary). Preschool Word Pop passes **`{ rate: 0.7 }`** where games previously used slower playback.

## Closing punctuation (? !)

Filenames omit **`?`** (e.g. **`how are you.png`**). When the **Turkish** gloss ends with **`?`** or **`!`** and the English label does not already end with that character, **`mirrorClosingPunctuationFromTurkish`** appends it — e.g. **`Nasılsın?`** → displayed/spoken English **`…YOU?`**.

Keep Turkish gloss punctuation honest for curriculum questions so English stays aligned.

## Wire-up checklist

- Resolve the vocab row: **`const entry = vocabulary.find((x) => x.word === gridWord)`**.
- Labels: **`getWordPopDisplayWord(gridWord, entry?.file, entry?.turkish)`** (not raw **`entry.word`** when basename carries spaces / nicer wording).
- Audio: **`speakWordPopAnswer(gridWord, entry?.file, entry?.turkish)`** or with **`{ rate: 0.7 }`** for preschool.

## Anti-patterns

- **`new SpeechSynthesisUtterance(balloon.word)`** or **`speakWord(compressedKey)`** without **`wordPopSpeak`**.
- Duplicating **`file.replace(/\\.png$/i).toUpperCase()`** display helpers instead of **`getWordPopDisplayWord`** (loses Turkish **`?!`** mirroring and diverges from Spell Quest basename rules).
